<title>JAPAN: Dollar rises to 92-month high versus mark in Tokyo.</title>
<headline>Dollar rises to 92-month high versus mark in Tokyo.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>0315 GMT	     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT</p>
<p> USD/JPY     117.25/30		   117.41-116.83</p>
<p> USD/DEM     1.8455/65		   1.8465-1.8380</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The dollar rose a 92-month high versus the mark by Tokyo midday on Monday, as lingering fears of a weak and broad-based single European currency continued to fuel speculative purchases of dollars for marks, traders said.</p>
<p>The dollar rose as high as 1.8465 marks, its highest level since November 1989, when the greenback reached a peak of 1.8690/95 marks.</p>
</text>
